abstract: >-
  A family of North-East lattice paths from (0,0) to (n,n) in which any two
  paths share an even number of edges has at most 2^n members. We prove
  Shankar's conjecture that exactly C_n families attain this bound, one for
  each noncrossing perfect matching, by classifying all equality cases of
  the underlying inequality. We also compute the binary rank of every grid
  graph and bound parity families of paths in every rectangle.
